  "note": "Whole-council election of the Gilford Town Commissioners under the Elections and Franchise Act (Northern Ireland) 1946, polled Wednesday 18 September 1946. There were no nominations, so the sitting members continued (Banbridge Chronicle, 7 September 1946, p. 1). The report states that these nine were the present personnel of the Commissioners. Returned unopposed."
